direction: down

title: |md
  ## mprog: ordered multi-prog attach
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

problem: "Classic tc problem\n\nMany BPF progs on one hook?\nClassic tc used filter priorities:\n  - tc filter add ... pref 100 ...\n  - tc filter add ... pref 200 ...\n\nReorder = delete + re-add.\nNo atomic insert \"before X\"/\"after Y\".\nNo clean way to coordinate owners." {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
}

mprog: "mprog (multi-program) abstraction\n\nKernel infra from tcx, also used by netkit.\nProvides:\n  - bpf_link-based ownership\n  - flag-based ordering at attach time\n  - inspection: list attached progs\n\nFlags:\n  - BPF_F_BEFORE  — prepend before existing\n  - BPF_F_AFTER   — append after existing\n  - BPF_F_REPLACE — replace specific link\n  - BPF_F_LINK    — attach via link FD" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
}

example: "Example: chain three programs\n\nOrder: counter → fw → tracer\n\n  P1 (counter)  attach BEFORE\n  P2 (fw)       attach AFTER existing\n  P3 (tracer)   attach BEFORE existing → puts P3 first\n\nFinal order at runtime: P3 → P1 → P2\n\nEach program returns:\n  - TC_ACT_OK        continue chain\n  - TC_ACT_SHOT      drop, stop chain\n  - TC_ACT_REDIRECT  redirect, stop chain" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

problem -> mprog
mprog -> example
